          "options": {
            "content": "**Purpose** \u2014 hold the exporter's declared cost against its measured cost, so a cost declaration cannot quietly become fiction.\n\n**Read it in this order**\n\n1. Read budget used and the declared-against-measured graph.\n2. If measured exceeds declared, the configuration is under-stating cost \u2014 fix the declaration or the interval.\n3. If measured is pinned to the enforced ceiling, collection intervals are effectively longer than configured.\n\n**When something is red**\n\n- Duty cycle high: find the dominant view in **Statement cost** and lengthen its scan window or its interval.\n- Throttling non-zero: the exporter is already holding itself back; freshness on the pipeline dashboard will show the cost.\n\n**Related dashboards** \u2014 Collection pipeline, Triage, Capacity\n\n*Owner: set this to the team that answers the page. Runbook: link it here \u2014 a red panel with no runbook is a puzzle, not an alert.*",
